    "text": "ADB approves a $250 million loan for Pakistan! 🏗️\nAccording to Dawn, the Asian Development Bank on Wednesday approved a $250 million policy-based loan to help Pakistan strengthen its public-private partnership (PPP) system and build a pipeline of bankable, sustainable projects. The financing supports reforms to prepare market-ready, cost-efficient infrastructure projects and improve fiscal risk management. It is the second phase of the Promoting Sustainable Public-Private Partnerships Programme; with ADB support, the government has approved a medium-term PPP pipeline for 2026-2030.\nCan public-private partnerships fix Pakistan's infrastructure gap? Tell us below 👇\n\nImage: AI-generated illustration.\n\n#RiseUpPakistan #ADB #Infrastructure #PakistanEconomy #PakistanNews",
